A||||22||Zoom88||Still having problems with idle, driving me nuts !!||||1||
Z||000000||Zoom88||12-09-2001||09:05 AM||||  At idle my motor (2.8) revs up and down around 2-300 rpms sometimes alittle more sometimes it quits for a few minutes. Also I have noticed it is becoming harder to start unless I give it a little gas while starting.<BR>It use to crank right up. Other wise it runs strong. Here is a list of things I have added to the motor and Items I have chaged out (not nessessarly because of this prob.)<BR> I recntly installed an Ocelot Exhaust system with no Cat (mainly because the old system was leaking everywhere and had to fix 3 broken manifold bolts) When I fixed the bolts I went ahead and cleaned up the manifolds for better flow.<BR> The car has new or replaced within the last year the following items:<BR>  MAP<BR>  TEMP. SENDER/SENSOR(for the gauge and light)<BR>  TEMP SENSOR - for the ECM<BR>  HYPERTECH CHIP, V-6 176 DEGREE FAN  SWITCH,160 DEGREE THERMOSTAT <BR>  ALTERNATOR<BR>  BATTERY<BR>  DECARBONIZED<BR>  DISTRIBUTER - Rebuilt<BR>  DISTRIBUTER cap and rotor -can't remember  brand but its red <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>  COIL - stock<BR>  FIERO SHOP SPARK PLUG WIRES <BR>  IAC - idle air control<BR>  TPS - throttle postioner sensor<BR>  K&N air filter<BR>  Can not find any vacuum leaks.<BR>  I am wondering if because of the more open exhaust I may need to install a adjustable Fuel Pressure regulator. (I am hunting for ideas here people !!)<BR>  Also I have a question about the TACH FILTER, if it goes bad will it effect the engine or just the TACH itself ?<BR>  I am also thinking maybe some bad injectors. <BR>  I get no codes. It did straighten up for awhile (day or two) when I replaced the MAP, and disconnected the battery for a few minutes to reset the ECM. <BR>  I am out of ideas.......Anyone?<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-09-2001||09:33 AM||||I've heard of such problems coming from a defective EGR valve.  I Didn't notice that in your list of replacements.<P>The HAYNES Fiero manual, shows pretty good ways of checking it. Although some of it seems tedious.<P>Maybe just replace it, see what happens. <P>The numbers on top of the EGR are important to as which kind to get. Somebody may have installed the wrong one?<P>A tech from West Coast Fiero had mentioned the EGR prob a couple of days ago, but I can't remember what thread it was under.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||Zoom88||12-09-2001||09:50 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>I've heard of such problems coming from a defective EGR valve.  I Didn't notice that in your list of replacements.<P>The HAYNES Fiero manual, shows pretty good ways of checking it. Although some of it seems tedious.<P>Maybe just replace it, see what happens. <P>The numbers on top of the EGR are important to as which kind to get. Somebody may have installed the wrong one?<P>A tech from West Coast Fiero had mentioned the EGR prob a couple of days ago, but I can't remember what thread it was under.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>  Does anyone know about this ? If I go to my local parts store and ask for an EGR for an 88 Fiero 2.8 will it be the correct one ?<BR>I am going to go read up on it in the service manual, Thanks <P><p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-09-2001||09:55 AM||||The haynes manual mentions "negative" backpressure and "positive" backpressure.<P>The numbers on top identify which type.<P>With all your upgrades, maybe the needs of EGR have changed???<P>Just a guess, I'm not a technician, just read a lot!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>Wheres that West Coast Fiero Tech!!!!!<p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
